From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PROPOSAL] Keep safe-fault watchdog recovery independent of logging

The ARM64 safe-fault caller enters terminal WFI after this callback. Optional
snapshot disablement must not skip the existing emergency watchdog request.
Preserve the enabled-logging path and existing raw watchdog count. This is a
recovery correction, not a fix for the initiating corruption or proof that it
caused any observed device hang. Not in the automatic boot patch chain.

--- a/drivers/trace/exynos-ss.c
+++ b/drivers/trace/exynos-ss.c
@@ -2207,13 +2207,15 @@
 	size_t len;
 
 	if (unlikely(!ess_base.enabled))
-		return;
+		goto reset;
 
 	strncat(text, cpu_num[cpu], 1);
 	len = strnlen(text, SZ_32);
 
 	exynos_ss_report_reason(ESS_SIGN_SAFE_FAULT);
 	exynos_ss_dump_panic(text, len);
+reset:
+	/* Fault recovery must not depend on optional snapshot logging. */
 	s3c2410wdt_set_emergency_reset(100);
 
 }
